{
  "title": "11: Hud هود",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓرٰ كِتٰبٌ اُحْكِمَتْ اٰيٰتُهٗ ثُمَّ فُصِّلَتْ مِنْ لَّدُنْ حَكِيْمٍ خَبِيْرٍۙ‏(1)\nALAARAA KETAABUM AUHKEMAT AAYAATOHU SUMMA FUSSELAT MIN LADUN HAKEEMIN KHABEERIN.\nAlif Lam Ra. (A L. R.) (this is) a book whose verses are firmly arranged (together) then separated (in revelation) from the All-Wise, the All-A ware.\nاَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّنِىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ وَّبَشِيْرٌ ۙ‏(2)\nALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA LAAHA INNANEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM WWABASHEERUN.\nThat ye should worship not (any one) but God; Verily I am for you from Him, a Warner and a bearer of good tidings.\nوَّاَنِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُمَتِّعْكُمْ مَّتَاعًا حَسَنًا اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى وَ يُؤْتِ كُلَّ ذِىْ فَضْلٍ فَضْلَهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ كَبِيْرٍ‏(3)\nWA ASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE YUMATTEA’KUM MATAA-A’N HASANAN ELAA ELAA AJALIM WA YUTE KULLA ZEE FAZLIN FAZLAH WA TAWALLAW FA-INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN KABEER.\nAnd (to preach unto you) that “Seek ye the forgiveness of your Lord, then turn ye unto Him repentant, He will provide you with a goodly provision to an appointed term and bestow on every gracious one endowed with grace; and if ye turn back, then verily I fear for you the torment of an awful day.\nاِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(4)\nELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nUnto God is your return; and He over all things hath power.\nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ يَثْنُوْنَ صُدُوْرَهُمْ لِيَسْتَخْفُوْا مِنْهُؕ اَلَا حِيْنَ يَسْتَغْشُوْنَ ثِيَابَهُمْۙ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَۚ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(5)\nALAA INNAHUM YASNOONA SUDOORAHUM LEESTAKHFOOA MENHU ALAA HEENA YASTAGHSHOONA SEEABAHUM YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA MAA YO’LENOON INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nBehold! Verily they fold up their breasts that they may conceal (their infidelity) from Him; Behold! when they put their garments as a covering knoweth He what (all) they conceal and what (all) they make known; verily knoweth He (all the inmost secrets) of the breasts.\nوَمَا مِنْ دَآ بَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ رِزْقُهَا وَ يَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَاؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(6)\nWA MAA MIN DAABBATINW WA FIL ARZE ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE REZQUHAA WA YA’LAMO MUSTAQARRAHAA WAMUSTAWDAA’AHAA KULLUL FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThere is no moving creature in the earth but on God is its sustenance, And He knoweth its resting-place and its repository; All (things) is in the Manifest Book.\nوَ هُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَ يَّامٍ وَّكَانَ عَرْشُهٗ عَلَى الْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ اَيُّكُمْ اَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا ؕ وَلَئِنْ قُلْتَ اِنَّكُمْ مَّبْعُوْثُوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الْمَوْتِ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(7)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FEE SETTATE A’ZAABAN YYAAMIN WA KAANA A’ARSHUH A’LAL AL-MAAE LE-YABLOWAKUM AYYOKUM AHSANO A’AMALAN WA LAIN QULTA INNAKUM MAB-O’OSOONA MIN BA’DE MAWT LAYAQOOLANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nAnd He it is Who created the heavens and the earth in six days - And His Throne was on the water - (He created the Heavens and the earth) that He might try you, which of you is best in conduct; And if thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) sayest, “Verily ye shall be raised up after death,” surely would say those who disbelieve: “This is (not) but open sorcery.\nوَلَئِنْ اَخَّرْنَا عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابَ اِلٰٓى اُمَّةٍ مَّعْدُوْدَةٍ لَّيَقُوْلُنَّ مَا يَحْبِسُهٗؕ اَلَا يَوْمَ يَاْتِيْهِمْ لَيْسَ مَصْرُوْفًا عَنْهُمْ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA LAIN AAKKHARNAA A’NHOMUL A’ZAABA ELAA UMMATIN MMAA’DOODATIN LLAYAQOOLUNNA MAA YAHBESUH ALAA YAWMA YAATEEHIM LAYSA MASROOFAN A’NHUM WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd if We hold back from them the torment until a reckoned time, they will surely say: “What holdeth it back?” Beware! on the day it cometh to them it shall not be turned away from them, and will encircle them that which they used to scoff at.\nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنَّا رَحْمَةً ثُمَّ نَزَعْنٰهَا مِنْهُۚ اِنَّهٗ لَيَئُوْسٌ كَفُوْرٌ‏(9)\nWA LAIN AZAQNAN INSAANA MINNAA RAHMATAM SUMMA NAZAA’NAAHAA MINHO INNAHU LAYAOOSUN KAFOORUN.\nAnd if We make man taste mercy from Us, (and) then take it off from him; Verily he is despairing, ungrateful.\nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنٰهُ نَعْمَآءَ بَعْدَ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ ذَهَبَ السَّيِّاٰتُ عَنِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَفَرِحٌ فَخُوْرٌۙ‏(10)\nWA LAIN AZAQNAAHO NAA’MAAA BA’DA ZARAAA-A MASSATHO LAYAQOOLANNA ZAHABAL AS-SAYAAATU A’NNEE INNAHU LAFAREHUN FAKHOORUN.\nAnd if We make him taste (Our) favours after distress hath afflicted him, he will surely say: “The evils have (all) gone away from me;” Verily he is joyous, boastful\nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nILLAA LAZEENA SABAROO WA A’MELUS AS-SAALEHAATE OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN KABEER.\nExcept those who forbear and do good; these! for them is forgiveness and a recompense (very) great.\nفَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكٌۢ بَعْضَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَضَآئِقٌ ۢ بِهٖ صَدْرُكَ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ جَآءَ مَعَهٗ مَلَكٌ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ نَذِيْرٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ ؕ‏(12)\nFALAA’ALLAKA TAAREKUN YAWM MAA YOOHAA ELAYKA WAZAAEQUN BEHI SADRUKA AN YAQOOLOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE KANZUN AW JAAA-A MA-A’HU MALAKUN INNAMAA ANTA NAZEERUM WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\nSo perchance mayest thou (be inclined) to give up a part of what is revealed unto thee and becometh straitened thy breast by it lest they say: “Why hath not a treasure been sent down unto him or an angel come with him?” (Say thou that) Verily thou art only a warner; and God over all things is the Custodian!\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِعَشْرِ سُوَرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ مُفْتَرَيٰتٍ وَّ ادْعُوْا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(13)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL FAATOO BEA’ASHRE SOORIN MISLEH MUFTARAYTIN WA O’O MANIS ENIS TA-TA’TUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nOr do they say: “He (Our apostle) hath forged it.” Say thou! “Bring ye then ten suras like unto it forged, and call ye (to your aid) whomsoever ye can besides God, if ye be truthful.\nفَاِلَّمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ بِعِلْمِ اللّٰهِ وَاَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(14)\nFAALLAM YASTAJEEBOO LAKUM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA UNZELA BEE’ELME LAAHE WA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA HAL ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\nThen if they answer ye not, then know ye that this (Qur’an) is revealed (only) by God’s knowledge, and that there is no god but He! Will ye then submit (and be Muslims now?).\nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا وَ زِيْنَتَهَا نُوَفِّ اِلَيْهِمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فِيْهَا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا لَا يُبْخَسُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO HAYAATAD DUNYAA WA ZEENATAHAA NOOFFE ELAYHIM A-A’MAALAHUM FEEHAA WA HUM FEEHAA LAA YUBKHASOONA.\nWhosoever desireth the life of this world and its pomp, We shall pay them (the recompense for) their deeds therein, they shall suffer not any loss.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا النَّارُ ۖ  وَحَبِطَ مَا صَنَعُوْا فِيْهَا وَبٰطِلٌ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LAYSA LAHUM FEE AAKHERATE ILLAA TAMASSANAN WAHABETA MAA SANAU’OOA FEEHAA WABAATELUN MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThese are they for whom there is nothing in the hereafter but (the Hell) fire, and vain shall be (all) that they wrought in it, and vain shall be what they were doing.\nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ وَيَتْلُوْهُ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْهُ وَمِنْ قَبْلِهٖ كِتٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِمَامًا وَّرَحْمَةً  ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهٖ مِنَ الْاَحْزَابِ فَالنَّارُ مَوْعِدُهٗ ۚ فَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْهُ اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(17)\nAFAMAWN KAANA A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN RABBEHI WAYATLOOHU SHAAHEDUN MINHO WA MIN QABLEHI KETAABU MOOSAA AEMAAMAN WA RAHMATAL OOLAAA-EKA YOAMENOONA BEHI WA MAN YAKFUR BEHI MENAL AL-AAHZAABE FANNAARO MAWE’EDUH FALAA TAKU FEE MIRYATIM MINHO INNAHUL HAQQO MIN RABBEKA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOONA.\nIs he then (like unto him) who hath a clear proof from his Lord and followeth him a witness from Him, and preceded by the Book of Moses, a guide and a mercy (testifying it)? These believe in it; and whosoever of the parties (of the idolaters) disbelieveth in it, the (Hell) fire is the promised place; so be thou not in doubt about it; verily it (Qur'an) is the truth from thy Lord; but most of the people believe not.\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ وَ يَقُوْلُ الْاَشْهَادُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ ۚ اَلَا لَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN OOLAAA-EKA YUA’RAZOONA A’LAA RABBEHIM WA YAQOOLO AL-AASHHAADU HAAOOLAAA-E LAZEENA KAZABOOA A’LAA RABBEHIM ALAA LA’NATUL LAAHE A’LAL ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God? These shall be presented before their Lord, and shall say the witnesses: “These are those who lied against their Lord; Beware! (Now) verily the curse of God is on the unjust\nالَّذِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ؕ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nLAZEENA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAYABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\nThose who hinder (others) from the path of God and seek to make it crooked; and they in the hereafter, they are the disbelievers.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا مُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ۘ يُضٰعَفُ لَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ ؕ مَا كَانُوْا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَمَا كَانُوْا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(20)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAM YAKOONOOA MUA’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AAWLEEAAAA YUZAAA’AFU LAHOMUL A’ZAABO MAA KAANOO YASTATEE-O’ONA JA-A’LA WA MAA KAANOO YUBSEROON.\nThese shall in no way weaken (God’s design) in the earth nor shall there be for them besides God any protecting friends; The torment shall be doubled for them; They could not bear to hear and they used not to see.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(21)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThese are they who have lost their selves and have left them (in lurch) (the false deities) what they (fancifully) used to forge.\nلَا جَرَمَ اَ نَّهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْاَخْسَرُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA JARAMA A’ZAABAN NNAHUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL AKHSAROON.\nUndoubtedly they are the very ones who in the hereafter will be the greatest losers.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاَخْبَتُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(23)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAAKHBATOOA ELAA RABBEHIM OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JANNAH HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nVerily those who believe and do good and humble themselves unto their Lord, these are the dwellers of the Garden (Paradise), they will abide therein.\nمَثَلُ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ كَالْاَعْمٰى وَالْاَصَمِّ وَالْبَصِيْرِ وَالسَّمِيْعِ ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيٰنِ مَثَلًا ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(24)\nMASALUL AL-FAREEQAYNE KA-A-A’MAA WAL AASAMME WAL BASEERE WAALSSAMEEE’E HAL YASTAWEENE MASALAA AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThe similitude of the two parties is like the blind and the deaf, and the seeing (ones) and the hearing (ones): What! Can they two be (compared as) equals? Will ye not then mind?\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(25)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI INNEE LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nAnd indeed sent We Noah unto his people (and he said unto them) “I am unto you a plain warner.\nاَنْ لَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(26)\nAN LAA TA’BODOO ILLAA LAAH INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN ALEEM.\nThat ye shall worship not (any one) but God; verily I fear for you the chastisement of a painful day.\nفَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا نَرٰٮكَ اِلَّا بَشَرًا مِّثْلَنَا وَمَا نَرٰٮكَ اتَّبَعَكَ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِىَ الرَّاْىِۚ وَمَا نَرٰى لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ فَضْلٍۢ بَلْ نَظُنُّكُمْ كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(27)\nFAQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA NARAAKA ILLAA BASHARAN MMESLANAA WA MAA NARAAKA ATTABAA’AKA ILLAA LAZEENA HUM AARAAZELUNAA BAADEAAA AR-RAAAAE WA MAA NARAA LAKUM A’LAYNAA MIN FAZLIN BAL NAZUNNUKUM KAAZEBEENA.\nThen said the chiefs of those who disbelieved from among his people: “We see not (in) thee but a man like ourselves and we see not any have followed thee but those who are the meanest of us, at first thought (without discretion), nor see we (in) you any excellence over us, nay we deem you liars.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖ فَعُمِّيَتْ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اَنُلْزِمُكُمُوْهَا وَاَنْتُمْ لَهَا كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WAATAANEAA RAHMATAM MIN I’NDEHI FAU’UMMEET A’LAYKUM AANULZEMUKUMOOHAA WA ANTUM LAHAA KAAREHOONA.\nSaid he: “O’ my people! think ye, if I be upon a clear proof from my Lord, and He hath bestowed on me mercy from unto Himself and it hath been made obscure unto you; shall we compel you to (accept) it while ye be averse from it?\nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مَالًا ؕاِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ مُّلٰقُوْا رَبِّهِمْ وَلٰكِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ قَوْمًا تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MAALAWN AEN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA MAA ANAA BETAAREDE LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAHUM MOLAAQOO RABBEHIM WALAAKENNEAA AARAAKUM QAWMAN TAJHALOON.\nAnd, O’ my people! I ask not of you any wealth in return for it; my reward is (with none) but with God and I will drive not away those who believe; verily they shall meet their Lord, but I see you a people (who act) ignorantly.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ طَرَدتُّهُمْؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI MAN YYANSURUNEAA MENAL LAAHE IN TARADTTUHUM AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nAnd, O’ my people! Who will help me against God if I drive them away! What! will ye not then mind?\nوَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ خَزَآئِنُ اللّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ وَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ اِنِّىْ مَلَكٌ وَّلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَزْدَرِىْۤ اَعْيُنُكُمْ لَنْ يُّؤْتِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ خَيْرًا ؕ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ ۖۚ اِنِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM E’ENDEAA KHAZAAENUS LAAHE WA LAA A-A’LAMO GHAYBA WA LAA AAQOOLU INNEE MALAKUN WA LAA AAQOOLU LILLAZEENA TAZDAREAA AAA’YUNUKUM LAN YYUTEEHUMU LAAHO KHAYRAN ALLAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE ANFOSEHIM INNEE EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd I say not unto you that with me are the treasures of God; and I know not the unseen, nor say I that I am an angel; and say I not about those whom your eyes hold in contempt (that) God will never bestow on them (any) good; God knoweth best what is in their hearts, for verily then I should be of the unjust ones.\nقَالُوْا يٰنُوْحُ قَدْ جَادَلْتَنَا فَاَكْثَرْتَ جِدَالَنَا فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏ ‏(32)\nQAALOO YAANOOHU QAD JAADALTANAA FAAKSARTA JEDAALANAA FAATENAA BEMAA TAE’EDUNAA IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nSaid they: “O’ Noah! indeed hast thou disputed with us and thou hast prolonged the dispute with us, now bring thou unto us what thou hast threatened us with, if thou art of the truthful ones.\nقَالَ اِنَّمَا يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِهِ اللّٰهُ اِنْ شَآءَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA INNAMAA YAATEEKUM BEHIL LAAHO IN SHAAA-AL WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nSaid he: “Verily God will bring it unto you only if He willeth, and ye shall by no means prevail against Him.\nوَلَا يَنْفَعُكُمْ نُصْحِىْۤ اِنْ اَرَدْتُّ اَنْ اَنْصَحَ لَكُمْ اِنْ كَانَ اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّغْوِيَكُمْؕ هُوَ رَبُّكُمْ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَؕ‏(34)\nWA LAA YANFAU’UKUM NUSHEAA IN AARADTTU AN AANSAHA LAKUM IN KAANA LAAHO YOREEDO AN YYUGHWEEKUM HOWA RABBOKUM WA ELAYHE TURJAU’OONA.\nAnd will profit you not my good advice, if I intend to give you good advice if God willeth that He should leave you astray; He is your Lord! and unto Him (only) shall ye be returned.\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ اِنِ افْتَرَيْتُهٗ فَعَلَىَّ اِجْرَامِىْ وَاَنَا بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(35)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL ENIS AFTARAYTUH FA A’LAYYA AEJRAAMEAA ANAT BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUJREMOONA.\nOr say they: “He (Muhammad) hath forged it (Qur’an)? Say thou! If I have forged it, on me be my guilt, and I am free of that which ye are guilty.\nوَاُوْحِىَ اِلٰى نُوْحٍ اَنَّهٗ لَنْ يُّؤْمِنَ مِنْ قَوْمِكَ اِلَّا مَنْ قَدْ اٰمَنَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ ۖ  ۚ‏(36)\nWA OOHEYA ELAA NOOHIN ANNAHU LAN YYUMENA MIN QAWMEKA ILLAA MAN QAD AAMANA FALAA TABTAES BEMAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd it was revealed unto Noah: that “never will any of thy people believe except those who have already believed, therefore grieve thou not for what they do\nوَاصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(37)\nWAASNAE’E AL-FULKA BEAAA’YUNENAA WAWAHYENAA WA LAA TUKHAATEBNEAA FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\nAnd make thou an ark under Our eyes and Our revelation and thou address (plead) not unto Me about those who are unjust; Verily they shall be drowned.\nوَيَصْنَعُ الْفُلْكَ وَكُلَّمَا مَرَّ عَلَيْهِ مَلَاٌ مِّنْ قَوْمِهٖ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُؕ قَالَ اِنْ تَسْخَرُوْا مِنَّا فَاِنَّا نَسْخَرُ مِنْكُمْ كَمَا تَسْخَرُوْنَؕ‏(38)\nWAYASNAU’U AL-FULKA WA KULLAMAA MARRA A’LAYHE MALAA MIN QAWMEHI SAKHEROOA MENHU QAALA IN TASKHAROOA MINNAA FAINNAA NASKHARU MINKUM KAMAA TASKHAROONA.\nAnd he began making the Ark; and whenever the chiefs of his people passed by him, mocked they at him; Said he: “If ye mock at us, verily we too shall mock at you, even as ye mock (at us).\nفَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(39)\nFA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA YAHILLO A’LAYHE A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\nSoon shall ye know who it is on whom descendeth a torment which will disgrace him, and on whom (ultimately) falleth a lasting torment.\nحَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُۙ قُلْنَا احْمِلْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ وَمَنْ اٰمَنَؕ وَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ مَعَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(40)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA WAFAARA AT-TANNOORU QULNAL AHMEL FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNE NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHE QAWLO WA MAN AAAMANA WA MAA AAMANA MA-A’HU ILLAA QALEELUN.\nUntil when came Our command and water gushed forth out of the oven, said We: “Carry (thou O’ Noah) in it two of each kind, a pair, and thy family, except him on whom the sentence hath already been passed, and those who believe”. And there believed not with him but a few.\nوَقَالَ ارْكَبُوْا فِيْهَا بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ مَجْرٖؔٮٰھَا وَمُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ ‏(41)\nWA QAALA ARKABOOA FEEHAA BISMIL LAAHE MAJRA WAMURSAAHAA INNAL RABBEE LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nAnd said he (Noah): “Embark ye in it, In the name of God be its sailing and its anchorage! Verily my Lord is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَهِىَ تَجْرِىْ بِهِمْ فِىْ مَوْجٍ كَالْجِبَالِ وَنَادٰى نُوْحُ اۨبْنَهٗ وَكَانَ فِىْ مَعْزِلٍ يّٰبُنَىَّ ارْكَبْ مَّعَنَا وَلَا تَكُنْ مَّعَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA HEYA TAJREE BEHIM FEE MAWJIN KA-JEBAALE WANAADAA NOOHU ABNAH KAANAL FEE MAA’ZELIN YYAABUNAA ARKAB MMAA’ANAA WA LAA TAKUN MA-A’L KAAFEREEN.\nAnd it (the Ark) moved on with them amid waves (towering) like mountains; and Noah called out unto his son: and he was aloof, “O’ My son! embark (thou) with us and be not with the disbelievers.\nقَالَ سَاٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى جَبَلٍ يَّعْصِمُنِىْ مِنَ الْمَآءِؕ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ الْيَوْمَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَۚ وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِيْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA SAAWEAA ELAA JABALIM YYAA’SEMUNEAA MENAL AL-MAAE QAALA LAA A’AASEMA YAWMA MIN AMRE LAAHE ILLAA MAN RAHEMAL WAHAALA BAYNAHOMAA AL-MAWJU FA KAANA MENAL AL-MUGHRAQEENA.\nSaid he “I will betake me unto a mountain that shall secure me from the water;” Said he (Noah): “There is no protector today from God’s decree but (of whom) He hath mercy;” and a wave passed between them, so he was among the drowned (ones).\nوَقِيْلَ يٰۤاَرْضُ ابْلَعِىْ مَآءَكِ وَيٰسَمَآءُ اَقْلِعِىْ وَغِيْضَ الْمَآءُ وَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ وَاسْتَوَتْ عَلَى الْجُوْدِىِّ وَقِيْلَ بُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(44)\nWA QEELAD YAARZU ABLAE’EAA MAAAKE WAYSAMAAU AAQLEE’EAA WAGHEEZA AL-MAAU WA MIN WAASTAWAT A’LAL AL-JOODEAAAE WA QEELAD BUA’DAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd it was said: “O’ Earth! swallow down thy water, and O’ sky! withhold (thy rain)! And the water abated, and the decree was fulfilled, and it (the Ark) rested on the (Mount) Judi; and it was said “Away with the unjust people!\nوَنَادٰى نُوْحٌ رَّبَّهٗ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ ابْنِىْ مِنْ اَهْلِىْ وَاِنَّ وَعْدَكَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنْتَ اَحْكَمُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(45)\nWANAADAA NOOHUN RRABBAH FAQAALA RABBE INNAL ABNEAA MIN AAHLEAA WA INNA WAA’DAKA HAQQO WA ANTA AAHKAMU HAAKEMEEN.\nAnd Noah cried unto his Lord and said: “My Lord! Verily my son is of my family; and verily Thy promise is true, and Thou art the most just of the judges.\nقَالَ يٰنُوْحُ اِنَّهٗ لَيْسَ مِنْ اَهْلِكَ ۚاِنَّهٗ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ ۖ فَلَا تَسْئَلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَعِظُكَ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(46)\nQAALA YAANOOHU INNAHU LAYSA MIN AAHLEKA INNAHU A’AMALUN GHAYRO SAALEHIN FALAA TASALNE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUM INNEE AAE’EZUKA AN TAKOONA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nSaid, He (God): “O’ Noah! Verily he is not of thy family; Verily he is (of) conduct other than righteous; There fore seek thou not of Me that of which thou hast no knowledge; Verily I admonish thee lest thou mayest be of the ignorant ones.\nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَسْئَلَكَ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌؕ وَاِلَّا تَغْفِرْ لِىْ وَتَرْحَمْنِىْۤ اَكُنْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(47)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE A-OO’ZO BEKA AN AASALAKA MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI E’ELMUN WA ILLAA TAGHFER LEE WATARHAMNEAA AAKUN MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nSaid he: “O’ My Lord! Verily I seek refuge in Thee from asking Thee that of which I have no knowledge; And if Thou forgiveth me not and have mercy on me, I should be of the losers.\nقِيْلَ يٰنُوْحُ اهْبِطْ بِسَلٰمٍ مِّنَّا وَبَرَكٰتٍ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّمَّنْ مَّعَكَؕ وَاُمَمٌ سَنُمَتِّعُهُمْ ثُمَّ يَمَسُّهُمْ مِّنَّا عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(48)\nQEELA YAANOOHU AHBET BESALAAMIN MINNAA WABARAKAATIN A’LAYKA WA A’LAA OMAMIN MIMMAYN MMAA’AKA WA OMAMUM SANUMATTEU’UHUM SUMMA YAMASSUHUM MINNAA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nIt was said: “O’ Noah! Debark thou with peace from Us and blessings on thee and on the people (the springs) of those with thee; and there shall be (other) people whom We shall afford provisions, then shall afflict them from Us a painful torment.\nتِلْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهَاۤ اِلَيْكَۚ مَا كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُهَاۤ اَنْتَ وَلَا قَوْمُكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ هٰذَا ۛؕ فَاصْبِرْ ۛؕ اِنَّ الْعَاقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(49)\nTILKA MIN AANBAAE GHAYBE NOOHEEHAA ELAYKA MAA KUNTA TAA’LAMUHAA ANTA WA LAA QAWMUKA MIN QABLE HAAZAA FAS-BIR INNAL AL-A’AAQEBATA LILMUTTAQEEN.\nThese are of the tidings of the unseen which We reveal unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad); thou didst not know them thou (thyself) nor thy people (knew it) ere this; Therefore be thou patient; Verily the end is (only) for the pious ones.\nوَاِلٰى عَادٍ اَخَاهُمْ هُوْدًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا مُفْتَرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA ELAA A’ADIN SAMOODA HOODAN QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH IN ANTUM ILLAA MUFTAROONA.\nAnd unto (the people) ‘Ad (We sent) their brother Hud. Said he: “O’ my people! Worship ye (the Only) God, ye have no god other than He; ye are but forgers.\nيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا ؕ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى الَّذِىْ فَطَرَنِىْ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nLE-QAWMEHI LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAZEE FATARANEE AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nO’ my people! I ask you not on it any recompense; my recompense is only with Him Who created me; What! then ye understand not?\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُرْسِلِ السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّيَزِدْكُمْ قُوَّةً اِلٰى قُوَّتِكُمْ وَلَا تَتَوَلَّوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(52)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI ASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE YURSELE SAMAAA-AD A’LAYKUM MMEDRAARAN WWAYAZEDKUM QUWWAH ELAA QOOTEKUM WA LAA IN MUJREMEEN.\nAnd O’ my people! Ask ye the forgiveness of your Lord and then turn ye repentant unto Him, He sendeth clouds on you pouring down abundant rain and addeth He strength to your strength, and turn ye not back as guilty ones.\nقَالُوْا يٰهُوْدُ مَا جِئْتَنَا بِبَيِّنَةٍ وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِتٰرِكِىْۤ اٰلِهَتِنَا عَنْ قَوْلِكَ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(53)\nQAALOO YAAHOODU MAA JETANAA BE-BAYYENAH WA MAA NAHNO BETAAREKEAA AAALEHATENAA A’N QAWLEKA WA MAA NAHNO LAKA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nSaid they: “O’ Hud! thou hast not brought unto us any clear sign (of your truthfulness) and we will desert not our gods on thy word! and nor are we believers in thee!\nاِنْ نَّقُوْلُ اِلَّا اعْتَرٰٮكَ بَعْضُ اٰلِهَتِنَا بِسُوْٓءٍ ؕ قَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُشْهِدُ اللّٰهَ وَاشْهَدُوْۤا اَنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ ۙ‏(54)\nIN NNAQOOLU ILLAA AA’TARAAKA BA’ZUL AAALEHATENAA BE-SOOO-IN QAALA INNEE AUSHHEDU LAAHA WAASHHADOOA AANNEAA BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\nWe say nothing but that have smitten thee some of our gods with evil;” said he: “Verily I call God to witness, and bear ye also witness that I am clear of what ye associate,\nمِنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَكِيْدُوْنِىْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ لَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(55)\nMIN DOONEHI FAKEEDOONEAA JAMEE-A’A SUMMA LAA TUNZEROONE.\nBesides Him, and then conspire ye against me all of you and give ye no respite.\nاِنِّىْ تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ رَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ ؕ مَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ اٰخِذٌ ۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(56)\nINNEE TAWAKKALTU A’LAL LAAHE RABBEE WA RABBEKUM MAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL ILLAA HOWA AAAKHEZUN BENAASEETEHAA INNAL RABBEE A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nVerily I rely on God, my Lord and your Lord; there is no living creature but He holdeth it (in His control) by its forelock; Verily my Lord is on the Right path.\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ مَّاۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖۤ اِلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَيَسْتَخْلِفُ رَبِّىْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْۚ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْنَهٗ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيْظٌ‏(57)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQAD AABLAGHTUKUM MAA AURSELTU BEHI ELAYKUM WAYASTAKHLEFU RABBEE QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM WA LAA TAZURROONAH SHAY-ANW INNAL RABBEE A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HAFEEZUN.\nBut if ye turn back, then indeed have I conveyed unto you that which I have been sent with unto you, and my Lord will make to succeed you, people other than you; and ye can not do harm unto Him in any way at all; Verily my Lord is over all things the (ever) Protecting.\nوَ لَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا هُوْدًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَ نَجَّيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ غَلِيْظٍ‏(58)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL HOODAN WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WA NAJJAYNAAHUM MIN A’ZAABIN GHALEEZ.\nAnd when Our decree came (to pass), We delivered Hud and those who believed with him by a mercy from Us; and We delivered them from a (very) severe torment.\nوَتِلْكَ عَادٌ جَحَدُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَصَوْا رُسُلَهٗ وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ كُلِّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍ‏(59)\nWA TILKAL A’ADUN JAHADOOA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM WAA’ASAWA ROSOLAHU WAT TABA-O’O AAMRA KULLE JABBAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\nAnd this was (the people) ‘Ad, they denied the signs of their Lord, and disobeyed His apostles, and followed the bid dings of every insolent tyrant.\nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ عَادًا كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّعَادٍ قَوْمِ هُوْدٍ‏(60)\nWAATBEU’OOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA LA’NAH WWAYAWMA AL-QEEMATE ALAA INNAL A’AADAN KAFAROO RABBAHUM ALAA BUA’DAN LLEA’AADIN QAWME HOODIN.\nAnd they were followed in this world by a curse and on the Resurrection Day (also); Behold! verily (the people) ‘Ad disbelieved in their Lord; Behold! away with ‘Ad the people of Hud.\nوَاِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًاۘ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ هُوَ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاسْتَعْمَرَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَاسْتَغْفِرُوْهُ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ قَرِيْبٌ مُّجِيْبٌ‏(61)\nWA ELAA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH HOWA AN-SHA-A MENAL ARZE WAASTAA’MARAKUM FEEHAA FAASTAGHFEROOHU SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE INNAL RABBEE QAREEB MMUJEEBUN.\nAnd unto the (people) Thamud (sent We) their brother Salih. Said he: “O’ my people’! Worship ye (none but the only) God; Ye have no god other than He; He raised you from the earth and hath given you to flourish therein; therefore ask ye forgiveness of Him, then turn ye repentant unto Him: Verily my Lord is (ever) Nigh, (ready) Responser.\nقَالُوْا يٰصٰلِحُ قَدْ كُنْتَ فِيْنَا مَرْجُوًّا قَبْلَ هٰذَآ اَتَنْهٰٮنَاۤ اَنْ نَّعْبُدَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَاِنَّنَا لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ مُرِيْبٍ‏(62)\nQAALOO YAASAALEHU QAD KUNTA FEENAA MARJOOA QABLA HAAZAA AATANHAANAA AN NNAA’BUDA MAA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA WA INNANAA LAFEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA TAD-O’ONAA ELAYHE MOREEB.\nSaid they: “O’ Salih! Indeed thou wert amongst us in whom (our) hopes were centred before this; Dost thou (now) forbid us from worshipping what our fathers did worship? And verily we are in a disquieting doubt about that unto which thou callest us.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ مِنْهُ رَحْمَةً فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ عَصَيْتُهٗ فَمَا تَزِيْدُوْنَنِىْ غَيْرَ تَخْسِيْرٍ‏(63)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WAATAANEAA MINHO RAHMATAM FAMAN YYANSURUNEAA MENAL LAAHE IN A’ASAYTUH FAMAA TAZEEDOONANEAA GHAYRA TAKHSEERIN.\nSaid he: “O’ my people! See ye not? if I am on a clear sign (guidance) from my Lord and He hath granted mercy (His apostleship) from Himself, who will then help me against God if I disobeyed Him? Therefore ye add not to my lot (anything) other than loss.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةُ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اٰيَةً فَذَرُوْهَا تَاْكُلْ فِىْۤ اَرْضِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ قَرِيْبٌ‏(64)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI HAAZEHI NAAQATU LAAHE LAKUM AAYATAL FAZAROOHAA TAAKUL FEE AARZE LAAHE WA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOOO-IN FAYAAKHUZAKUM A’ZAABUN QAREEB.\nAnd O’ my people! This is God’s she camel for you, a sign (of my truthfulness), there fore leave her to (freely) pasture on God’s earth and ye touch her not with (any) evil, for then will overtake you a ready torment.\nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوْا فِىْ دَارِكُمْ ثَلٰثَةَ اَ يَّامٍ ؕذٰ لِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوْبٍ‏(65)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FAQAALA TAMATTAU’OOA FEE DAAREKUM SALAASATA A’ZAABAN YYAAMIN ZAA LEKA WAA’DUN GHAYRO MAKZOOBIN.\nYet they did hamstring her, Then said he “Enjoy ye in your abode for three days; That is a promise not to be belied.\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا صٰلِحًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَمِنْ خِزْىِ يَوْمِئِذٍؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْقَوِىُّ الْعَزِيْزُ‏(66)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL AKHAAHUM WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WA MIN KHEZAAE YAWMEEZIN INNAL RABBAKA HOWA QAWIYYUL A’ZEEZUL.\nWhen Our decree came (to pass), We delivered Salih and those who believed with him by mercy from Us, and (We delivered them) from ignominy of that day; verily thy Lord, He is the Strong, the Mighty.\nوَاَخَذَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(67)\nWAAKHAZA LAZEENA ZALAMOOA AS-SAYHATU FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nAnd seized those who were unjust the (mighty) blast so they became in their homes motionless corpses,\nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ ثَمُوْدَا۟ كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُوْدَ‏(68)\nKA-AN LAM YAGHNAWA FEEHAA ALAA INNAL SAMOODAA KAFAROO RABBAHUM ALAA BUA’DAN LLESAMOODA.\nAs though they dwelt not in them; Behold! Verily (the people) Thamud disbelieved in their Lord; Behold! verily away with (the people) Thamud.\nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ بِالْبُشْرٰى قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ فَمَا لَبِثَ اَنْ جَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ حَنِيْذٍ‏(69)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA IBRAAHEEMA BIL-BUSHRAA QAALOO SALAAMAA QAALA SALAAMUN FAMAA LABESA AN JAAA-A BEE’EJLIN HANEEZIN.\nAnd indeed Our messengers (the angels) came unto Abraham with glad tidings; Said they: “Peace! (Abraham in reply), said (And on you also be) “Peace”! and delayed not to bring a roasted calf.\nفَلَمَّا رَاٰۤ اَيْدِيَهُمْ لَا تَصِلُ اِلَيْهِ نَكِرَهُمْ وَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً  ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِ لُوْطٍ ؕ‏(70)\nFALAMMAA RAA AYDEYAHUM LAA TASELU ELAYHE NAKERAHUM WAAWJASA MINHUM KHEEFATAN QAALOO LAA TAKHAF INNAA AURSELNAA ELAA QAWME LOOTIM.\nBut when he saw that their hands extended not towards it, (he) mistrusted them and conceived fear of them. Said they (the Angels): “Fear (thou) not; Verily we are sent unto Lot’s people.\nوَامْرَاَ تُهٗ قَآئِمَةٌ فَضَحِكَتْ فَبَشَّرْنٰهَا بِاِسْحٰقَ ۙ وَمِنْ وَّرَآءِ اِسْحٰقَ يَعْقُوْبَ‏(71)\nWAAMRAA RA-ATOHU QAAEMATUN FAZAHEKAT FABASSHARNAAHAA BE-ISHAAQA WA MIN FAS-ALOOHUNNA ISHAAQA YA’QOOBAL.\nAnd his wife was standing (by), and she laughed, then We gave her the glad tidings of Isaac and after Isaac of (a son’s son) Jacob.\nقَالَتْ يٰوَيْلَتٰٓى ءَاَلِدُ وَاَنَا عَجُوْزٌ وَّهٰذَا بَعْلِىْ شَيْخًا ؕ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَشَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‏(72)\nQAALAT YAAWAYLATAAA AALEDU ANAT A’AJOOZUN WWAHAAZAA BAA’LEAA SHAYKHAN INNAL HAAZAA LASHAAUN A’AJEEBUN.\nSaid she: “O’ Woe unto me! shall I bear a son (now) when I am an (extremely) old (woman) and this my husband an (extremely) old (man)? Verily this is a thing wonderful!\nقَالُوْۤا اَتَعْجَبِيْنَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ رَحْمَتُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكٰتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِؕ اِنَّهٗ حَمِيْدٌ مَّجِيْدٌ‏(73)\nQAALOO AATAA’JABEENA MIN AMRE LAAHE RAHMATU LAAHE WABARAKAATUH A’LAYKUM AHLAL AL-BAYTE INNAHU HAMEED MAJEEDUN.\nSaid they: “What! wonderest thou at the decree of God? The mercy of God and His blessings be on ye, O’ People of the House; Verily He (alone) is Praiseworthy, the All-Glorious!\nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبَ عَنْ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الرَّوْعُ وَجَآءَتْهُ الْبُشْرٰى يُجَادِلُنَا فِىْ قَوْمِ لُوْطٍؕ‏(74)\nFALAMMAA ZAHABAL A’N IBRAAHEEMA AR-RAWU’U WA JAAA-ATHO AL-BUSHRAA YUJAADELUNAA FEE QAWME LOOTIN.\nAnd when had gone away from Abraham the awe and the glad tidings came unto him, he began pleading with Us for Lot’s people.\nاِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَحَلِيْمٌ اَوَّاهٌ مُّنِيْبٌ‏(75)\nINNAL IBRAAHEEMA LAHALEEMUN AAWAHUN MMUNEEBUN.\nVerily Abraham was indeed forbearing, compassionate, oft- returning (to God).\nيٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ اَعْرِضْ عَنْ هٰذَا ۚ اِنَّهٗ قَدْ جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَ ۚ وَاِنَّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِمْ عَذَابٌ غَيْرُ مَرْدُوْدٍ‏(76)\nYAABRAAHEEMU AAA’REZ A’N HAAZAA INNAHU QAD JAAA-A AMRUL RABBEKA WA INNAHUM AAATEEHEM A’ZAABUN GHAYRO MARDOODIN.\nO’ Abraham! Forsake this! Indeed the decree of thy Lord hath come to pass; and verily unto them cometh a torment (which is) irreversible.\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَا لُوْطًا سِىْٓءَ بِهِمْ وَضَاقَ بِهِمْ ذَرْعًا وَّقَالَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَصِيْبٌ‏(77)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA LOOTAA SEEE-A BEHIM WA ZAAQA BEHIM ZAR-A’NW WA QAALA HAAZAA YAWMUL A’ASEEBUN.\nAnd when Our messengers (the angels) came unto Lot, he was grieved for them and felt his arm straitened to protect them and said: “This is a distressful day.\nوَجَآءَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ يُهْرَعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ ؕ وَمِنْ قَبْلُ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ بَنٰتِىْ هُنَّ اَطْهَرُ لَكُمْ ۚ فَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُخْزُوْنِ فِىْ ضَيْفِىْ ؕ اَلَيْسَ مِنْكُمْ رَجُلٌ رَّشِيْدٌ‏(78)\nWA JAAA-AHU QAWMOHU YUHRAU’OONA ELAYHE WA MIN QABLO KAANOO YA’MALOON SAYYE-AATE QAALA LE-QAWMEHI HAAOOLAAA-E BANAATEAA HUNNA ATHARO LAKUM FAT-TAQUN LAAHA WA LAA TUKHZOONE FEE ZAYFEAA A-LAYSA MINKUM RAJOLUM RRASHEEDUN.\nAnd came his people rushing unto him; for aforetime they did evil deeds; Said he (Lot): “O’ my people! these my daughters are - they are purer for you, so guard ye against (the punishment of) God, and disgrace me not about my guests; Is there not among you a single man rightminded?\nقَالُوْا لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا لَنَا فِىْ بَنٰتِكَ مِنْ حَقٍّ ۚ وَاِنَّكَ لَتَعْلَمُ مَا نُرِيْدُ‏(79)\nQAALOO LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA LANAA FEE BANAATEKA MIN HAQQIN WA LATAA’LAMU MAA NOREEDO.\nSaid they: “Indeed knowest thou that we need not thy daughters, and verily well-knoweth thou what we intend.\nقَالَ لَوْ اَنَّ لِىْ بِكُمْ قُوَّةً اَوْ اٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى رُكْنٍ شَدِيْدٍ‏(80)\nQAALA LAW ANNAL LEE BEKUM QUWWAH AW AAAWEAA ELAA RUKNIN BAA-SIN.\nSaid he: “Would that I had strength to resist you or betake myself to a strong supporter.\nقَالُوْا يٰلُوْطُ اِنَّا رُسُلُ رَبِّكَ لَنْ يَّصِلُوْۤا اِلَيْكَ فَاَسْرِ بِاَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِّنَ الَّيْلِ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ اَحَدٌ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَكَؕ اِنَّهٗ مُصِيْبُهَا مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْؕ اِنَّ مَوْعِدَهُمُ الصُّبْحُؕ اَلَيْسَ الصُّبْحُ بِقَرِيْبٍ‏(81)\nQAALOO YAALOOTU INNAA RUSULU RABBEKA LAN YYASELOOA ELAYKA FA-ASRE BEAAHLEKA BEQETA’IN MENAL LAYLE WA LAA YALTAFET MINKUM AHAD ILLAA AMRAATAKA INNAHU MUSEEBUHAA MAA AASAABAHUM INNAL MAWE’EDAHUMU AS-SUBHU A-LAYSA AS-SUBHU BE-QAREEBIN.\nSaid they: “O’ Lot! Verily we are messengers from thy Lord! Never shall they reach thee! so depart thou with thy people while a part of the night remaineth, and let none of you turn back - but thy wife; Verily shall befall her what befalleth them; Verily their appointed time is the morning; Is not the morning nigh?\nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا جَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا حِجَارَةً مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍۙ  مَّنْضُوْدٍۙ‏(82)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA JA-A’LNAA A’AALEEHAA SAAFELAHAA 58 WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHAA HEJAARATAN MIN SIJJEELIN MANZOODIN.\nSo when Our decree came to pass, We turned their (township) upside down, and rained on them hard stones of baked clay, (spreading) layer on layer.\nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَؕ وَ مَا هِىَ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(83)\nMMUSAWMATAN I’NDAL RABBEKA WA MAA HEYA MENAL ZAALEMEEN BE-BA-E’ED.\nMarked (for punishment) with thy Lord; Nor are they (the ruins of their township) far distant from the unjust ones.\nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ وَلَا تَنْقُصُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ بِخَيْرٍ وَّاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ مُّحِيْطٍ‏(84)\nWA ELAA MADYANA SAMOODA SHO-A’YBAA QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH WA LAA TANQUSOOA AL-MEKYAALA WA MEEZAAN INNEE AARAAKUM BE-KHAYRIN WWAANNEAA AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN MMUHEETIN.\nAnd unto (the people of) Midian (We sent) their brother Shu’aib. Said he: “O’ my people! Worship ye God (alone); Ye have no god other than He; and give not short measure and weight, Verily I see you in prosperity and verily I fear for you the torment of an all-encompassing day.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اَوْفُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(85)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI AAWFOOA AL-MEKYAALA WA MEEZAAN BIL QISTE WA LAA TABKHASOOA NAASA AASHYAAAHUM WA LAA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd O’ my people! give ye full measure and (correct) weight in justice, and defraud ye not people of their things, and act not corruptly in the earth, making mischief.\nبَقِيَّتُ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ  ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَفِيْظٍ‏(86)\nBAQEETU LAAHE KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEHAFEEZIN.\nThat which is left by God unto you is good for you if ye be believers, and I am not over you a keeper.\nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ اَصَلٰوتُكَ تَاْمُرُكَ اَنْ نَّتْرُكَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ نَّفْعَلَ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِنَا مَا نَشٰٓؤُا ؕ اِنَّكَ لَاَنْتَ الْحَلِيْمُ الرَّشِيْدُ‏(87)\nQAALOO YAASHUA’AYBU AASALAAWTUKA TAAMURUKA AN NNATRUKA MAA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA AW AN NNAFA’ALA FEE AAMWAALENAA MAA NASHAAAUA INNAKA LAANTA AL-HALEEMU AR-RASHEEDU.\nSaid they: “O’ Shu’aib! Doth thy religion enjoin thee that we should forsake what our fathers did worship or we (should forsake to) do with our property what we please? Forsooth thou art the one forbearing, the rightminded.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَرَزَقَنِىْ مِنْهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا ؕ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُخَالِفَكُمْ اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْهٰٮكُمْ عَنْهُ ؕ اِنْ اُرِيْدُ اِلَّا الْاِصْلَاحَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ ؕ وَمَا تَوْفِيْقِىْۤ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ‏(88)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WARAZAQANEAA MINHO RIZQAN HASANAN WA MAA OREEDO AN AUKHAALEFAKUM ELAA MAA AANHAAKUM A’NHO IN OREEDO ILLAA AL-AESLAAHA MAA ASTATAA’TU WA MAA TAWFEEQEAA ILLAA BIL-LAAHE A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE AUNEEBU.\nSaid he: “O’ my people! See ye not if I am on a clear sign (guidance) from my Lord, and (He) hath provided me from Himself, sustenance (pure and) good; and I desire not that in opposition to you I betake my self unto that which I forbid you from it; I desire naught but reform what I am able to (do); and my guidance is not but with God; On Him (alone) do I rely, and unto Him (alone) do I turn.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شِقَاقِىْۤ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمْ مِّثْلُ مَاۤ اَصَابَ قَوْمَ نُوْحٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ هُوْدٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ صٰلِحٍؕ وَمَا قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ مِّنْكُمْ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(89)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHEQAAQEAA AN YYUSEEBAKUM MMESLU MAA ASAABA QAWMA NOOHIN AW QAWMA HOODIN AW QAWMA SAALEHIN WA MAA QAWMO LOOTIM MINKUM BE-BA-E’ED.\nAnd, O’ my people! Let not (your) opposition to me cause you to sin, lest befalleth unto you the like of what befell the people of Noah, or the people of Hud, or the people of Salih; and nor the people of Lot are far off from you.\nوَاسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ رَحِيْمٌ وَّدُوْدٌ‏(90)\nWAASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA AELAYHE INNAL RABBEE RAHEEMUN WWADOODUN.\nAnd ask ye forgiveness of your Lord, and turn ye unto Him (repentant); Verily my Lord is All-Merciful, Loving-Kind.\nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ مَا نَفْقَهُ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا تَقُوْلُ وَاِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِيْنَا ضَعِيْفًا ۚ وَلَوْلَا رَهْطُكَ لَرَجَمْنٰكَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْنَا بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(91)\nQAALOO YAASHUA’AYBU MAA NAFQAHU KASEERAA MIMMAA TAQOOLO WA INNAA LANARAAKA FEENAA HAQQO WA LAWLAA RAHTUKA LARAJAMNAAKA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYNAA BEA’AZEEZIN.\nSaid they: “O’ Shu’aib We understand not much of what thou sayest, and most surely we see thee weak amongst us; and were it not for thy family we would surely stone thee; and thou art not against us powerful.\nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَهْطِىْۤ اَعَزُّ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُ وَرَآءَكُمْ ظِهْرِيًّا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(92)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI AARAHTEAA AAA’AZZU A’LAYKUM MENAL LAAHE WA ATTAKHAZTUMOOHU WARAAAKUM ZEHREEA INNAL RABBEE BEMAA TA’MALOON MOHEETUM.\nSaid he: “What! Is my family more esteemed by you than God? and caste ye Him behind your back, with neglect? Verily, my Lord encompasseth what (all) ye do.\nوَيٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌ ؕ سَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَمَنْ هُوَ كَاذِبٌ ؕ وَارْتَقِبُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ رَقِيْبٌ‏(93)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA MAN HOWA KAAZEBUN WAARTAQEBOOA INNEE MA-A’KUM RAQEEBUN.\nAnd O’ my people! Act ye according to your ability, I too am acting; soon will ye know on whom cometh the torment that will disgrace him, and who it is a liar; and watch ye, verily I too with you am watching.\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا شُعَيْبًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَاَخَذَتِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(94)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL SHO-A’YBAA WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WAAKHAZATE LAZEENA ZALAMOOA AS-SAYHATU FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nAnd when came to pass Our decree We delivered Shu’aib and those who believed with him by mercy from Us; and overtook those who did injustice, the (mighty) blast so they became in their homes motionless corpses,\nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّمَدْيَنَ كَمَا بَعِدَتْ ثَمُوْدُ‏(95)\nKA-AN LAM YAGHNAWA FEEHAA ALAA BUA’DAN LLEMADYANA KAMAA BAE’EDAT SAMOODO.\n(It happened) As though they dwelt not in them; Behold! away with (the people of) Midian even as were cast away (the people of) Thamud!\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(96)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nAnd indeed We sent Moses, with Our signs and an authority (which was) manifest,\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ ئِهٖ فَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ وَمَاۤ اَمْرُ فِرْعَوْنَ بِرَشِيْدٍ‏(97)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EH FA TABA-O’O WA AAMRA FIR-A’WNA WA MAA AMRUL FIR-A’WNA BERASHEEDIN.\nUnto Pharaoh and his chiefs, but they followed the bidding of Pharaoh; and Pharaoh’s bidding was no right directive.\nيَقْدُمُ قَوْمَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَاَوْرَدَهُمُ النَّارَؕ وَبِئْسَ الْوِرْدُ الْمَوْرُوْدُ‏(98)\nYAQDUMU QAWMAH YAWMA QEYAAMATE FAAWRADAHUMU AN-NAARA WA BEASAL AL-WERDU AL-MAWROODU.\nHe shall lead his people on the Resurrection Day, and bring them down to the (Hell) fire; but woeful will be the leading and the place led to.\nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهٖ لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ بِئْسَ الرِّفْدُ الْمَرْفُوْدُ‏(99)\nWAATBEU’OOA FEE HAAZEHI LA’NAH WWAYAWMA QEYAAMATE MASALUL AR-REFDU AL-MARFOODU.\nThey are followed by a curse in this (life) and (also) on the Day of Resurrection; And woeful is the gift which shall be given (unto them).\nذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْقُرٰى نَقُصُّهٗ عَلَيْكَ مِنْهَا قَآئِمٌ وَّحَصِيْدٌ‏(100)\nZAA LEKA MIN AANBAAE KORAA NAQUSSUH A’LAYKA MINHAA QAAEMUN WWAHASEEDUN.\nThis is of the account of (the fate of) the townships We relate unto thee (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) of them some are standing and some have been mown down (by the passage of time)\nوَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَغْنَتْ عَنْهُمْ اٰلِهَتُهُمُ الَّتِىْ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ لَّمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَؕ  وَمَا زَادُوْهُمْ غَيْرَ تَتْبِيْبٍ‏(101)\nWA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKIL ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAMAA AAGHNAT A’NHUM AAALEHATUHUMU LATEE YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN LAMMAA JAAA-A AMRUL RABBEKA WA MAA ZAADOOHUM GHAYRA TATBEEBIN.\nAnd We did no injustice unto them, but they were unjust unto themselves, so availed them not aught their gods whom they called upon besides God when came to pass the decree of thy Lord; they added not (aught to their lot) but perdition.\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَخْذُ رَبِّكَ اِذَاۤ اَخَذَ الْقُرٰى وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ ؕ اِنَّ اَخْذَهٗۤ اَلِيْمٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(102)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAKHZU RABBEKA EZAA AAKHAZA KORAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN INNAL AAKHZAH ALEEM SHADEEDUN.\nSuch is the grasp (of punishment) of thy Lord when graspeth He the townships while they are unjust; Verily His grasp (punishment) is painful, severe.\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّمَنْ خَافَ عَذَابَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّجْمُوْعٌ  ۙ  لَّهُ النَّاسُ وَذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّشْهُوْدٌ‏(103)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEMAN KHAAFA A’ZAABAL AAKHERATE ZAA LEKA YAWMUL MMAJMOOA’UN LLAHU NAASO WAZAA LEKA YAWMUL MMASHHOODUN.\nVerily, in this there is a sign for him who feareth the chastisement of the hereafter; This is a day for which mankind shall be gathered together, And this day shall be witnessed (by all)\nوَمَا نُؤَخِّرُهٗۤ اِلَّا لِاَجَلٍ مَّعْدُوْدٍؕ‏(104)\nWA MAA NUAKKHERUH ILLAA LE-ELAA MMAA’DOODIN.\nAnd We delay it not but to an appointed term.\nيَوْمَ يَاْتِ لَا تَكَلَّمُ نَفْسٌ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖۚ فَمِنْهُمْ شَقِىٌّ وَّسَعِيْدٌ‏(105)\nYAWMA TAKOONOO LAA TAKALLAMU NAFSUN ILLAA BE-IZNEH FA-MINHUM SHAQEAAAUN WWASAE’EEDUN.\nThe day (when) it arriveth, no soul shall speak but by His leave; then (some) of them shall be wretched and (some) blessed.\nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ شَقُوْا فَفِى النَّارِ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا زَفِيْرٌ وَّشَهِيْقٌ ۙ‏(106)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA SHAQOOA FA FIL NAAR LAHUM FEEHAA ZAFEERUN WWASHAHEEQUN.\nThen as for those who shall be wretched, they shall be in the (Hell) fire, for them therein shall be sighing and groaning.\nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ فَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ‏(107)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL ILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL RABBOKA INNAL RABBAKA FAAA’AALUN LEMAA YOREEDO.\nThey shall abide therein so long as the heavens and the earth endure, except (as) what willeth thy Lord; Verily thy Lord is the (Mighty) Doer of what soever He willeth.\nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ سُعِدُوْا فَفِى الْجَنَّةِ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ عَطَآءً غَيْرَ مَجْذُوْذٍ‏(108)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA SUE’EDOOA FA FIL JANNAH KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL ILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL RABBOKA A’TAAA-AN GHAYRA MAJZOOZIN.\nAnd as for those who will be blessed, they shall be in the garden (of Paradise) abiding therein so long as the heavens and the earth endure, except (as) what thy Lord willeth; (it will be) A gift incessant.\nفَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّمَّا يَعْبُدُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ؕ مَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا كَمَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُؕ وَاِنَّا لَمُوَفُّوْهُمْ نَصِيْبَهُمْ غَيْرَ مَنْقُوْصٍ‏(109)\nFALAA TAKU FEE MIRYATIM MIMMAA YAA’BUDU HAAOOLAAA-E MAA YA’BODOON ILLAA KAMAA YAA’BUDU AA-BAAA-OHUM MIN QABL WA WA INNAA LAMOOFFOOHUM NASEEBAHUM GHAYRA MANQOOSIN.\nTherefore be thou not in doubt concerning what worship these (people); they worship not but as their fathers did worship before (them); and verily We will certainly pay them back in full their (due) share without (any) rebate.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَاخْتُلِفَ فِيْهِ ؕ وَ لَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(110)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FAKHTOLEFA FEEHE WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM WA INNAHUM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nAnd indeed gave We unto Moses the Book, but variance was created in it; and had not a word (decree of respite) gone forth from thy Lord, the matter would surely have been decided between them; and verily they are in a doubt (about the Qur’an which is) disquieting (them).\nوَاِنَّ كُلًّا لَّمَّا لَيُوَفِّيَنَّهُمْ رَبُّكَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(111)\nWA INNA KULLAN LAMMAA LAYOOFFEENNAHUM RABBOKA A-A’MAALAHUM INNAHU BEMAA YA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nAnd verily unto all will thy Lord pay back in full their recompense for all their deeds; verily He of what (all) they do is fully aware.\nفَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَاۤ اُمِرْتَ وَمَنْ تَابَ مَعَكَ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(112)\nFAASTAQEM KAMAA AUMERTA WA MAN TAABA MA-A’KA WA LAA TATGHAW INNAHU BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nThen stand thou fast (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad) (on the Right Path) as thou art commanded (by thy Lord) and also he who hath turned (unto God) with thee, and (O’ men) be ye not inordinate; Verily He (your Lord), what ever ye do, well-seeth.\nوَلَا تَرْكَنُوْۤا اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا فَتَمَسَّكُمُ النَّارُۙ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA LAA TARKANOOA ELAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO FATAMASSAKUMU TAMASSANAN WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AAWLEEAAAA SUMMA LAA TUNSAROONA.\nAnd (ye believers) incline ye not unto those who act unjustly lest toucheth you the (Hell) fire, for you besides God there is no protector, nor shall ye be helped.\nوَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ طَرَفَىِ النَّهَارِ وَزُلَفًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ ؕ اِنَّ الْحَسَنٰتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ ذِكْرٰى لِلذّٰكِرِيْنَ ۚ‏(114)\nWA SALAATA TARAFAA AN-NAHAARE WAZULAFAN MENAL LAYLE INNAL AL-HASANAATE YUZHEBNA SAYYE-AATE ZAA LEKA ZEKRAA LELZZAAKEREENA.\nAnd establish thou, prayer in the two ends of the day, and at the approaches of the night, Verily the good deeds take away the evil deeds; This is a reminder for the (believers who are) mindful (of their Lord).\nوَاصْبِرْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(115)\nWAS BIR FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nAnd be thou patient, for verily God suffereth not to be lost the recompense of the righteous (ones).\nفَلَوْ لَا كَانَ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ اُولُوْا بَقِيَّةٍ يَّنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْفَسَادِ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ اَنْجَيْنَا مِنْهُمْ ۚ وَاتَّبَعَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مَاۤ اُتْرِفُوْا فِيْهِ وَكَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(116)\nFA LAW LAA KAANA MENAL QOROONE MIN QABLEKUM OOLOO BAQEETIN YYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-FASAADE FIL ARZE ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAYN AANJAYNAA MINHUM WA TABA-A’L LAZEENA ZALAMOO MAA AUTREFOOA FEEHE WA KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nBut why were not there among the generations before you those endowed with understanding forbidding against mischief in the earth, except a few of those whom We delivered from among them? And pursued those who did injustice, what they were made to enjoy (of the plenty) and they were guilty.\nوَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ لِيُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى بِظُلْمٍ وَّاَهْلُهَا مُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MAA KAANA RABBOKA LEEHLEKA KORAA BEZULMIN WWAAHLUHAA MUSLEHOON.\nNor was thy Lord (ever such) to destroy townships unjustly while its people were righteous.\nوَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَجَعَلَ النَّاسَ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلَا يَزَالُوْنَ مُخْتَلِفِيْنَۙ‏(118)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA LAJAA’ALA NAASA UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WA LAA YAZAALOONA MUKHTALEFEENA.\nAnd had thy Lord willed He would certainly have made men a single people, but they will cease not to differ,\nاِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَ رَبُّكَ ؕ وَلِذٰلِكَ خَلَقَهُمْ ؕ وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(119)\nILLAA MAN RAHEMAL RABBOKA WALEZAALEKA KHALAQAHUM WATAMMAT KALEMATU RABBEKA LAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MENAL JINNATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nExcept he on whom thy Lord hath mercy; And for this did He create them; and the word (decree) of thy Lord is fulfilled; Certainly will I fill the hell with the jinn and the men, all together.\nوَكُلًّا نَّقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الرُّسُلِ مَا نُثَبِّتُ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ ۚ وَجَآءَكَ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَقُّ وَمَوْعِظَةٌ وَّذِكْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(120)\nWAKULLAN NNAQUSSU A’LAYKA MIN AANBAAE AR-RUSULE MAA NUSABBETU BEHI FUAADAKA WA JAAA-AKA FEE HAAZEHE HAQQO WA MAW-E’ZATUM WA ZIKRAA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nAnd all that We relate unto thee of the accounts of the apostles is to confirm with it thy heart; And hath come unto thee in this the truth, and an admonition and a reminder unto the believers.\nوَقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْؕ اِنَّا عٰمِلُوْنَۙ‏(121)\nWA QUL LIL-LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNAA A’AMELOON.\nAnd say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) unto those who believe not; “Act (ye) whatever ye can: and verily we (too) do act.\nوَانْتَظِرُوْا ۚ اِنَّا مُنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWAANTAZEROOA INNAA MUNTAZEROONA.\nAnd wait ye! and verily we too do wait.\nوَلِلّٰهِ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُ الْاَمْرُ كُلُّهٗ فَاعْبُدْهُ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَيْهِؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(123)\nLILLAAHE GHAYBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA ELAYHE YURJAU’U MIN KULLUH FAAA’BUDHU WA TAWAKKAL A’LAYH WA MAA RABBOKA BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nAnd God’s is the unseen (worlds) of the heavens and the earth, and unto Him (only) is returned the whole of the affair, so worship thou (only) Him and rely thou (only) on Him; and thy Lord is not heedless of whatever ye do.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has a total of 123 verses. Imam Muhammad Baqir (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah every Friday, his accounts will on the Day of Judgement, be taken together with that of the Prophets and all his sins will be forgiven.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites Surah Hud will get a reward equal to the number of people who were there at the time of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his rank will be like of the martyrs. The accounting for his deeds will also be made easy for him.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that writing this Surah on a sheepskin and keeping it in one’s possession at all times makes one so courageous and bold that nobody can defeat him in combat. Whoever sees him will be filled with fear."
